  m_text: 'In the House of Wisdom in Baghdad, the polymath Al-Kindi noticed that
    every language uses some letters more than others. Count the symbols, match the
    most common to ''E'' or its equivalent, and any simple substitution unravels.


    <b>SIGNIFICANCE</b>

    Frequency
    analysis, the birth of cryptanalysis. For 600 years it made every monalphabetic
    cipher readable to a patient mind.'
