  _title: 
  _body: "Father-and-son cryptographers Antoine and Bonaventure Rossignol built a
    code of 587 numbers for the Sun King, some standing for syllables, some for letters,
    some as traps that deleted the previous symbol.\n\n<b>SIGNIFICANCE</b>\nSo strong
    that captured dispatches sat unread for 200 years, until \xC9tienne Bazeries
    finally solved it in the 1890s."
