  _bodyField: {fileID: 1631953749}
  _title: 
  _body: 'Polish mathematician Marian Rejewski attacked Enigma not with linguistics
    but with the theory of permutations, reconstructing its secret wiring from intercepted
    traffic alone.


    <b>SIGNIFICANCE</b>  The first break of the military Enigma,
    achieved years before the war, and handed to Britain and France in 1939 as the
    tanks rolled in.'
