  m_text: 'Whitfield Diffie and Martin Hellman solved the impossible: two people
    shouting across a crowded room can mix their colours of paint so that each ends
    with the same secret blend, while no listener can un-mix it.


    <b>SIGNIFICANCE</b>
    The first public-key idea ever published, ''New Directions in Cryptography''
    ended four thousand years of needing to share a key in advance.'
